# CITATION.cff — Citation File Format 1.2.0 (https://citation-file-format.github.io/)
# Verified against the live schema.json/schema-guide.md before writing this file.
#
# Known gaps, left as explicit TODOs rather than guessed at (do not silently invent these):
#   - `license`: omitted entirely. No LICENSE file exists in this repo yet (see README.md's own
#     "Do not treat this repo as licensed for reuse until one is added" note) -- adding an SPDX
#     license id here without a matching LICENSE file would be a false claim. Add both together.
#   - `authors[0]` uses CFF's `name:` (entity form) rather than a given/family split: the author
#     publishes as "Muhammed Muiz", a mononym-style byline with no separate family name, so
#     forcing a split would invent one. Matches paper.tex's \author{} exactly.
#   - `affiliation`: set to "Independent Researcher" per the PI's confirmation.
#   - `preferred-citation.url`/`identifiers`: arXiv ID is not yet assigned (PLAN.md §11/§7,
#     paper/paper.md §7 -- disclosure to MSRC/Alibaba is planned for arXiv-posting time, not sent
#     yet, so posting hasn't happened). Fill in the arxiv.org/abs/<ID> URL once posted.
#   - `date-released`: intentionally omitted -- set it to the actual v1.0-arxiv tag date at
#     release time (RUNBOOK.md's release steps), not before.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper (see preferred-citation) and, if
  referring to the pipeline/codebase itself, this repository.
title: >-
  jlens-fuzz: Judge-Shaped, Not Harm-Shaped: A Persistent Measurement-Validity Failure in
  Jailbreak Success Judges, and an Honest Null Result for Activation-Guided Mutation
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Muhammed Muiz"
    email: abdulmuiz3570@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
repository-code: "https://github.com/secslayer/jlens-fuzz"
url: "https://github.com/secslayer/jlens-fuzz"
abstract: >-
  Interpretability-guided jailbreak fuzzing for open-weight LLMs. Reports two findings: a
  measurement-validity failure in a widely-reused jailbreak success judge that persists after a
  deliberate fix (persona-wrapper false positives), and an honest null result for
  activation-guided span mutation vs. uniform mutation, with a mechanistic explanation grounded
  in refusal-direction separation quality. Full paper: paper/paper.tex (compiles to
  paper/paper.pdf); paper/paper.md is the markdown source of record it was derived from.
keywords:
  - jailbreak
  - LLM safety
  - red-teaming
  - interpretability
  - activation steering
  - refusal direction
  - judge reliability
  - AdvBench

preferred-citation:
  type: unpublished
  title: >-
    Judge-Shaped, Not Harm-Shaped: A Persistent Measurement-Validity Failure in Jailbreak Success
    Judges, and an Honest Null Result for Activation-Guided Mutation
  authors:
    - name: "Muhammed Muiz"
      email: abdulmuiz3570@gmail.com
      affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
  year: 2026
  # url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/XXXX.XXXXX"   # fill in once posted (paper/paper.md §7)
  notes: "arXiv preprint, not yet posted as of this file's creation (Gate 7 signed off; disclosure to MSRC/Alibaba planned for posting time, not yet sent -- see paper/paper.md §7 and reviews/stage7-human-signoff.md)."
